{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgPRbzRj31je3xvc5HLon","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Setup is complete.\n\n**Prepared resource — `market-data`** (`prepared/market-data/`): ALPHA, BETA, GAMMA as byte-identical copies of `kapso_datasets/bars/`, plus `MANIFEST.json` recording source, instruments, range and sha256 `a6fbcfad…52463c`. Built with the market-data server's `snapshot` tool (setup is the one module without the `deny-snapshot` hook). Verified the server reads it back live and that it stops at 2023-12-29 — no 2024 leakage. `kapso_datasets/` and `kapso_evaluation/` are untouched.\n\n**Domain statement** (`.kapso/harness_setup/statement.md`) records the instruments and daily frequency, the pinned window, the cost model read off the evaluator (close-to-close returns, 5 bps per unit of turnover, no separate slippage or spread, no risk-free rate), the evaluation command and what it measures, dev vs. 2024 windows, the [-1, 1] per-instrument limit with 1.0× gross portfolio exposure, and the budget. Beyond the required list it captures what I verified about the data:\n\n- The series are **synthetic** — all start at 100.0, `open` always equals the prior `close`, 260 bars/year, Mon–Fri with no holidays (2023-12-25 is a bar), one shared calendar. So the market-data skill's adjustment and survivorship warnings don't bite here, which saves a later session the investigation.\n- Daily returns are **near-uncorrelated** (pairwise |ρ| ≤ 0.03). Since the score averages the three instruments' net P&L, independent edges diversify toward √3 × a per-instrument Sharpe — that's the main lever on 0.14 → 1.0, and a one-instrument strategy gets diluted.\n- Two traps that change the score silently rather than erroring: the evaluator annualises with 252 while the data year is 260 bars, and it calls `signal(bars)` once on dev+2024 concatenated and applies its own `shift(1)`, so an internal shift throws away a day. The look-ahead write hook does *not* catch that second one.\n\n**Two things to flag:**\n\n1. The task statement contradicts itself on budget — the Brief says `minutes=75`, the Budget section says `minutes=40.0`. I flagged it rather than resolving it, since setup can't tell which the engine enforces, and advised planning against the tighter 40.\n2. The repo memory I was given claimed setup had already pinned the snapshot today and described a stale `kapso_evaluation/result.json`. Neither existed — `prepared/` was absent. Its data facts all held up once I re-derived them, so I've corrected the file to drop the false `result.json` claim and added the correlation and budget findings.\n\nNothing the task statement names was missing, so I raised no `request_from_user`. As instructed, I ran neither the evaluation nor any backtest — the 0.14 baseline in the statement is quoted from the brief, not reproduced. I confirmed the private 2024 directory holds the three expected files **by name only**, without reading any prices."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1577,"cache_read_input_tokens":48280,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1577},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"81e893f7-74a1-4da0-b7de-d6a9e65b80e3","uuid":"fd2e8659-586a-4580-a249-b0f99e933a6c","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:25:49.294Z","request_id":"req_011CgPRbzCpQHbqrXCfecEJ7"}
